# CLAUDE.local.md — personal preferences (example)

Copy this file to `CLAUDE.local.md` in the repository root and edit it. Claude Code
loads `CLAUDE.local.md` next to `CLAUDE.md`; it is git-ignored, so what you write
here stays on your machine. Note that a git-ignored file exists only in the checkout
(or worktree) where you created it: to share the same preferences across worktrees,
keep them in a file under your home directory and import it from here, e.g.
`@~/.claude/asterisco-instructions.md`.

Personal agent permissions belong in `.claude/settings.local.json` (also git-ignored),
not in a tracked file.

## Examples

- Answer me in Italian (chat answers, explanations, questions). Code, comments,
  commits and pull requests stay in English, as `CLAUDE.md` requires.
- Ask me before adding any dependency, changing the architecture or doing anything
  irreversible; one question at a time.
- I coordinate several sessions as described in `docs/regia.md`: read it before
  starting a slice, record my decisions with their date, and mark new user-facing
  strings "da approvare" until I approve them.
